    <section class="quiet-section"><h2>How practice is chosen</h2><p>FSRS-6 schedules each form toward 90% retention using standard learning steps. A first correct answer receives Good. Wrong or revealed answers receive Again. Accent differences are ignored and receive Good, just like exact answers; ñ remains distinct from n. Missing reflexive pronouns count as wrong.</p><p>New forms use frequency, first-attempt weaknesses, and occasional checks of less-practised categories. Related verbs test transfer after pattern errors. These introduction rules are transparent heuristics; they are not a validated curriculum.</p><p><a href="https://docs.ankiweb.net/manual/deck-options#fsrs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">About FSRS</a> · <a href="https://github.com/open-spaced-repetition/ts-fsrs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Scheduling library</a></p></section>
